{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Shared Seed Data Guardian",
  "description": "After a Spec task modifies seed data, mock data, member profiles, resources, events, or data shared across dashboards, review the implementation to ensure a single shared data source is maintained without duplication, with valid relationships, consistent references, and deterministic content.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "postTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A Spec task just completed. If the task modified seed data, mock data, member profiles, resources, events, or data shared across dashboards, review the implementation against these rules:\n\nSINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH:\nCommunityOS uses realistic frontend seed/mock data (src/mockData.js) instead of a real backend. This shared data model includes:\n- ~30 member profiles (Learners, Pros, Organizers)\n- ~15 learning resources/sessions\n- ~5 events with attendance and engagement numbers\n- ~2 detected topic gaps with radar scoring\n- Pro skills arrays\n- Pro \"Things I've helped with before\" (pastHelp)\n- Pro matching consent (openToMatch)\n- Previous learner matches\n- Learner help requests to Pros\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\nDo NOT create duplicated Pro/member data independently inside different dashboards or components.\n\nThe SAME Pro record must be usable by:\n- Pro dashboard (their own profile view)\n- Learner \"People who can help\" (matching results)\n- Organizer suggested people (gap recommendations)\n\nThe SAME \"Things I've helped with before\" data must drive evidence lines shown in all views.\nThe SAME \"Open to being matched with learners\" value must control visibility everywhere.\n\nRULES FOR MODIFYING SEED DATA:\n1. Preserve the shared schema (id, name, role, skills[], stuck, experienceLine, bio, roles[])\n2. Do NOT create duplicate hardcoded profiles in components\n3. Keep relationships valid (skills match radar topics, experienceLines match pastHelp)\n4. Keep references consistent (member IDs used in matches must exist in seedMembers)\n5. Do NOT randomly generate data at runtime if deterministic seed data is expected\n6. Keep enough data so dashboards are NEVER empty on initial load\n7. If new seed data is needed, add it to src/mockData.js (the shared source)\n8. Do NOT embed mock data inside individual page components\n9. Do NOT introduce a backend or database unless explicitly requested\n\nDATA CONSISTENCY CHECKS:\n- Every member ID referenced in matches/suggestions exists in seedMembers\n- Every skill tag used in matching exists in at least one member's skills[]\n- Every radar topic has at least one member with matching skills\n- Events, resources, and members form a coherent community picture\n- localStorage-persisted data (users, contributions, links) supplements but does not contradict seed data\n\nIf a change violates these rules:\n- Flag the specific violation (e.g., \"DashboardPage.jsx has hardcoded Pro data that duplicates seedMembers\")\n- Recommend moving the data to src/mockData.js\n- Do NOT perform unrelated refactoring\n- Do NOT consider the task complete until the data source is unified"
  }
}